This crate builds JohnnyGuitar NVSE (JohnnyGuitarNVSE.dll), the NVSE plugin, into nv-rs, with its
authors' permission (the maintainer, 2026-11-03: every mod author gave it). Source: JohnnyGuitar
NVSE, https://github.com/carxt/JohnnyGuitarNVSE, commit c87905e (VNV pins its release 5.28);
read: internal/JG/EditorIDRestoration.cpp, JohnnyExtraData and internal/JIP/JIPFixes.cpp's
InitLights. Its changes are rebuilt here from that source and the game's own code; no C++ is
included.

Credits: JohnnyGuitar NVSE is written by carxt and its contributors.

JohnnyGuitar NVSE is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1. nv-rs uses
it under section 3 of that licence, which lets a work be distributed under the GNU General Public
License instead; nv-rs is licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3, whose text is
this repository's LICENSE.

Gameplay commands additionally read from carxt/JohnnyGuitarNVSE at
59049a0c844111dab69aed372eb8e9c30f5cc5ae: JG/functions/fn_math.cpp (Clamp),
fn_utility.cpp (EditorIDToFormID), fn_gameplay.cpp (SendStealingAlarm),
fn_form.cpp (GetFactionFlags),
internal/JG/JohnnyCommands.cpp and matching parameter definitions.

JAM's command/event slice also uses that same 59049a0 source:
fn_form.cpp (GetBaseEffectAV, GetBaseEffectArchetype, GetCalculatedWeaponDPS),
fn_gameplay.cpp (TogglePipBoy, IsCrimeOrEnemy), fn_event.cpp,
events/{JohnnyEvents,EventFramework,LambdaVariableContext}.cpp and the matching
game-class and parameter declarations. Exact game call sites are documented in
docs/JAM.md; no C++ or executable bytes are included.
